<%#
  Story: the prose and the platform panel, two columns from lg up. No locals.

  The mockup fills one column with a workshop photograph that does not exist.
  An empty tinted rectangle 440px tall reads as a hole rather than as a
  composition, so that column carries the shape of the system instead.

  What the panel must not do is overstate it. This site does not read its own
  REST API: view routes render from the models directly, and the project's rules
  forbid a view route from depending on a JSON route. The API exists for the
  clients that are not this site. An earlier draft of this panel claimed every
  platform read the catalogue over the API, which was false in all three.

  A <dl> rather than a grid of divs — each row genuinely is a term and its
  description, and it linearises correctly for a screen reader.

  "Apps in progress" is deliberate. cluster3-project/mobile is still an empty
  directory, and announcing a shipped app would be the same invention the
  mockup's team section was dropped for.

  The prose comes first in the DOM and the panel is moved back into place with
  lg:order-first: a screen reader reaching the panel's heading before the
  heading of the section it supports reads backwards.
%>
<section class="grid items-center gap-10 py-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <div>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      A catalogue that stays the same everywhere
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Lpaecomms sells the peripherals people use all day: keyboards, mice, headsets, webcams,
      and the things around them. The whole catalogue is online, so you can browse it,
      compare, and decide without guessing.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      It is one store, not three. The site and the API the other platforms use read
      the same catalogue from the same place, so a product that changes shows up the
      same way wherever you opened it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-3xl bg-subtle p-8 lg:order-first">
    <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">One catalogue behind every platform</h2>
    <dl class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-5">
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">The catalogue</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          One source of products, shared by everything below.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Web</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          This site, rendered on the server straight from that source.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">The REST API</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The same products over HTTP, for clients that are not this site.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Mobile and desktop</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Apps in progress on that API.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
